Just an elaborate pointer.  Erwin S. Strauss, aka Filthy Pierre, has
something of a theory, or at least a hobbyhorse hypothesis, about this.
His catchphrase is PNP, or Post Nuclear Proliferation.

Filthy runs _The (Libertarian) Connection_ (TC), a paper discussion group
which I would describe as the best thing before the extropians list.
A couple of the other extropians came from there and could offer
opinions.  As I understand it, Filthy is also something of a figure
in SF fandom; maybe people have heard his PNP opinions that way.

Anyway, Filthy suggests that states as we know them will be way outnuked
and the world will divide into small Proprietary
Communities ("PCs") each owned by someone who can afford smuggled
nukes in other places, and thus able to defend its turf by threats
of nuclear recrimination.  PCs supposedly have this property that 
although their rules are set by their owners, the different PCs have
to compete for tenants on the basis of these rules, so here you have
a definite flavor of PPL, if somewhat feudal.

I'm not extremely well-versed in the details.  Filthy loves to talk
about these ideas, and because of that has to keep reminding people that
it isn't how he wants the world to go, just how he suspects it will.

I think he's written a book about it; he also wrote something called
"How to Start Your Own Country," I think.  I've let my subscription
to TC lapse but I could find his address if anyone's interested.

