Date:     Tue, 28 Dec 93 9:14:11 EST
From: cards@top.cis.syr.edu
Subject: Revolving US border doors

Canada and the US are about as tight as 2 countries can get.
Even highly classified military data can be shared with Canada
when it cannot be shared with any other nation.  Relations with
Mexico are nowhere near as good, but Mexico is not perceived
as much of a threat, and the border is long.

Try flying in and out of the US to interesting destinations,
you'll find security much tighter (although still laughable
for anyone with intelligence seriously trying to evade it).
The IRS, State Department, INS, Customs, InterPol and a few
other nice agencies have been collaborating for several
years now on setting up a computer network to facilitate
real-time checking of the papers and status of returning
US citizens.

"Mr. Jones, I see you have not filed with the IRS during
your year abroad... come with me."

Paranoia? Try reading some of the tax avoidance and
financial privacy (asset & income protection) newsletters,
some of which are written by former government (especially
IRS) agents.
