Subject:  IQ tests & abstract intelligence measurement

If you are interested in the debates over what constitutes
intelligence, how to measure its various dimensions and
what IQ tests measure, try Mensa.  Since their only
membership qualification is high IQ, they tend to believe
that IQ tests really do measure intelligence, but they
have their radicals who challenge this.  Otherwise I
find the group boring.  A typical Mensa meeting...

"Hello, superintelligent friends! What shall we discuss
today? Something new and different perhaps?"

"No, let's stick with the old standby: how intelligence
is the most important attribute in the world, how we
have more of it than anybody else, and how we will use
our superior brains to help the poor stupid masses
by designing more byzantine and expensive government
social programs!"

"OK, sounds great.  Now lets argue over little
nit-picking details without challenging any of
our major assumptions at all."

Uh... does this sound like anything else with which
extropian list readers might be familiar?
